{"kind":"request","text":"LC-1: the trust rows and the content bucket of `dap-lending`.\nThis is the second head of ruling d257a67f. It is its own small head.\nIt does not ride R. My act 196d99b7 gave both to R, and that was wrong.\n\nWhy: the hosted Lending and Counter installs and the NF-7 witness need\nthe two signed 0.2.0 releases only. They must not wait for R.\n\nWork, on main 57f887ce:\n1. Packets. Take the two blobs of the branch\n   planner/nf5-lending-counter-packets-20261114 at 64d3d6c1. Keep them\n   at `examples/lending/releases/0.2.0/application.dap.json` and\n   `apps/counter/releases/0.2.0/application.dap.json`. One rule covers\n   both applications: a signed packet lives under its version.\n2. Formatter. Add the two paths to `CANONICAL_PROTOCOL_PACKETS` in\n   `scripts/format-json.mjs` and to its test.\n3. Rows. `apps/room/wrangler.lending.jsonc` gets `APPLICATION_TRUST`\n   with two rows, each with release, publisher and host `github.com`:\n   Lending 93819e26 and Counter f681c1b5 of 196d99b7, publisher\n   key_qNT9aIt0WhJndvMP7UV33FFJ7DOYwW0JUvOv4PhNlFI.\n4. Bucket. The same file binds `APPLICATION_CONTENT` to the bucket\n   `dap-lending-application-content`. I create the bucket before I\n   deploy the head, and I say so in an act.\n5. Test, in `application-release-reproduction.test.ts`. Each row of\n   `dap-lending` has a packet in the tree. The published reader reads\n   the packet with the row's release, and the manifest publisher equals\n   the row's publisher. When the manifest version of a packet equals\n   the authored version of its application, the packet identifiers\n   equal the current `release-identifiers.json`. A difference fails\n   with words that tell the developer to raise the version.\n\nLimits. Add no copy of the identifiers file and no constants module\nfor 0.2.0. The packet holds its identifiers, and the row holds the\nrelease and the publisher. Name the reader first when one needs more.\nChange no screen host, no install context and no other Worker.\n\nGate. LC-1 takes the first gate slot after C3 at which its head is\nready. It displaces no head that holds a START. Then: the tooling\nhead, E1. Development runs take the idle slot under 5537a531.\n\nAfter the landing I create the bucket, deploy, and file the versions.\nThe installs and the NF-7 witness follow under their own requests.","body":{"conditions":"The head lands on main with the gate passed and the checker's approval. apps/room/wrangler.lending.jsonc names the two signed 0.2.0 releases and binds the content bucket. Both packets sit under their version paths. The reproduction test reads each row's packet and refuses changed identifiers at an unchanged version.","target_head":"57f887ce066448133d0bd0fe611d0935cc6eb0ed","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}